{"action_id":null,"arguments":[],"assumptions":[{"assumption_id":"node.a3bfe36da58bc7bb188e00cb.a0","provenance_refs":[],"statement":"The selected control concerns one corporation, one option transaction, one otherwise applicable margin obligation and one assessment date.","status":"PROVISIONAL"},{"assumption_id":"node.a3bfe36da58bc7bb188e00cb.a1","provenance_refs":[],"statement":"Actor classification and underlying regime applicability are distinct from membership in the circular's defined product category.","status":"PROVISIONAL"},{"assumption_id":"node.a3bfe36da58bc7bb188e00cb.a2","provenance_refs":[],"statement":"The collective definition applies non-central clearing to all three enumerated option categories.","status":"PROVISIONAL"},{"assumption_id":"node.a3bfe36da58bc7bb188e00cb.a3","provenance_refs":[],"statement":"The express commencement date governs the announced position; future amendment and gazettal are not added as unstated conditions precedent.","status":"PROVISIONAL"},{"assumption_id":"node.a3bfe36da58bc7bb188e00cb.a4","provenance_refs":[],"statement":"Unknown classification, underlying applicability and subsequent-notice facts remain unknown.","status":"PROVISIONAL"}],"bundle_hash":"eb17bfe36ff3690cd800661aebb8b22a96873ad46a029f3c708eb918c79173eb","candidate_id":"candidate.d5347a53da234b878ca464479a369f0c","controlled_language":"[TRUE_IS_SATISFIED] Within the scope of a licensed corporation and an otherwise applicable Part III of Schedule 10 margin obligation, true means the assessed transaction satisfies the proposed announced-exemption conditions: it is non-centrally cleared, belongs to one of the three listed option categories, is assessed on or after 4 January 2026, and the announcement remains applicable. False means at least one condition fails; it does not establish that margin is owed under other rules. Outside that scope this control supplies no applicability decision. Unknown facts remain unknown.","disposition_reason":"Unreviewed interpretation proposal","family_ids":["scope"],"generation_phase":"SHARED_RESOLUTION","issue_ids":[],"parent_id":"candidate.134e7b6d65e9477fa9447adc6f06b46e","probability_of_legal_correctness":null,"revision_reason":"The scope-and-definition challenge supports retaining the parent's substantive control. Being a licensed corporation does not itself establish that the margin regime otherwise applies; being an equity-linked instrument does not itself establish membership in the three defined option categories. The source does not support a rival extending eligibility to registered persons merely because they appear in the Code's title, restricting eligibility by an invented insignificant-exposure threshold, or requiring case-officer approval. Likewise, importing overseas qualifications or making gazettal a prerequisite lacks sufficient textual support. These failed hypotheses do not justify a second formalization. The strongest uncertainty is the missing Code's detailed actor and product scope. The reported incomparable fact bindings provide no substantive counterexample or basis for changing the preserved fact definitions.","run_id":"run.fb80a0de37cc42b091ce356d6e9e87d3","scheduling_priority":0,"schema_version":"interpretation.v1","score_purpose":"INVESTIGATION_PRIORITY_ONLY","source_packet_hash":"b0021963635f36e84bc1dbbeb387ab5373e66c36771dd2e73cd5daccefe89655","source_unit_ids":["d802c45a4262c.u0.0","d802c45a4262c.u1.381","d802c45a4262c.u15.1671","d802c45a4262c.u3.801","d802c45a4262c.u4.1019","d802c45a4262c.u6.1357","d802c45a4262c.u7.1479"],"status":"ACTIVE","subject_unit":"Applicability of the announced SFC equity-option margin exemption"}